WEBVTT

00:00:01.550 --> 00:00:03.549
Previously on Smallville.

00:00:03.549 --> 00:00:04.549
Lois, where is the orb?

00:00:04.549 --> 00:00:05.549
What a orb?

00:00:05.549 --> 00:00:07.549
The alien technology from my vault.

00:00:07.549 --> 00:00:10.550
You just want to take over the world with some alien nation.

00:00:10.550 --> 00:00:12.550
I am trying to save the world.

00:00:12.550 --> 00:00:18.550
My cousin Lois vanished for three weeks and then suddenly appeared claiming that she was being chased by a ninja-clad assassin.

00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:20.550
I think I know where she was.

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:21.550
The future.

00:00:21.550 --> 00:00:26.550
These for the dreams you've been having have something to do with your three weeks of blocked memory.

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:30.550
Why don't we have the powers we should have under yellow sun?

00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:35.549
I will find the answers we are looking for, or I will die in the quest.

00:00:35.549 --> 00:00:38.049
I give you the world's first solar tower.

00:00:38.049 --> 00:00:39.549
Are you risking your own life?

00:00:39.549 --> 00:00:42.549
Because it's the only chance I have before you destroy our world.

00:00:42.549 --> 00:00:46.549
Clark would never in a million years risk we needed to be done.

00:00:46.549 --> 00:01:02.560
And I told you Lois doesn't have that kind of time.

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:06.060
You get Dr. Weiss on a helicopter and get him to MetGen now.

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:10.060
Clerk, I got three of the country's best neuro-MDs on their way.

00:01:10.060 --> 00:01:12.060
It's too late. Lois is already missing.

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:13.060
What do you mean she's missing?

00:01:13.060 --> 00:01:14.060
You took her to the hospital.

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:15.060
You've been with her all night, Clark.

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:16.060
I was.

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:18.060
I stepped out to see if you called when I got back.

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:19.060
She was gone.

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:20.060
There's nothing in her chart.

00:01:20.060 --> 00:01:23.060
There's no releases and there are no witnesses.

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:26.060
Hospital said someone called and requested a copy of Lois's test results.

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:28.060
A meal.

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:30.060
Why would Emil care about Lois?

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:32.060
You wouldn't.

00:01:32.060 --> 00:01:36.780
Maybe the person he's working for would.

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:53.230
Chloe.

00:01:53.230 --> 00:01:56.230
Spying on Lois' computers and hacking any of her therapist files?

00:01:56.230 --> 00:01:59.230
Did you really need to escalate into kidnapping her from a coma ward?

00:01:59.230 --> 00:02:01.230
There's a mystery surrounding Miss Lane.

00:02:01.230 --> 00:02:04.230
this lane and this is my chance to solve it.

00:02:04.230 --> 00:02:06.230
So what, all this is because she told her shrinks,

00:02:06.230 --> 00:02:09.229
she has headaches and sees weird futuristic flashes?

00:02:09.229 --> 00:02:14.629
What? I can't hack in these files and not read them.

00:02:14.629 --> 00:02:16.629
They're called boundaries, Stewart. Find some.

00:02:16.629 --> 00:02:20.629
And these futuristic flashes may not be imaginary.

00:02:20.629 --> 00:02:24.629
Besides, Lois was investigating Zod's orb when she vanished for three weeks.

00:02:24.629 --> 00:02:27.629
Well, you think these are repressed memories that she's already been through?

00:02:27.629 --> 00:02:44.620
This technology will tell us.

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:46.620
Can't you get more than just fragments?

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:47.620
I'm sorry.

00:02:47.620 --> 00:02:50.620
but her mind is like a metal mosh pit right now, okay? Only a human...

00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:51.620
Pause it.

00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:58.030
That's a solid solar tower.

00:02:58.030 --> 00:03:04.240
Exactly as it's designed to be built.

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:06.240
But the plans haven't even gone public yet.

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:12.270
Lois did go to the future.

00:03:12.270 --> 00:03:16.270
Okay, well, I better pop some popcorn because she's remembering something.

00:03:16.270 --> 00:03:20.830
Where's the orb?

00:03:20.830 --> 00:03:33.099
What or? Where are you?

00:03:33.099 --> 00:03:35.099
Don't start what you can't finish!

00:03:35.099 --> 00:03:49.250
What the hell?

00:03:49.250 --> 00:05:05.519
Nothing but a filthy human.

00:05:05.519 --> 00:05:07.519
This zone is off limits to your kind.

00:05:07.519 --> 00:05:08.519
But this dream is all mine, so what's with the end?

00:05:08.519 --> 00:05:09.519
So what's with the attitude?

00:05:09.519 --> 00:05:12.519
It's not your place to ask questions.

00:05:12.519 --> 00:05:13.519
I'm a reporter.

00:05:13.519 --> 00:05:16.990
Asking questions is in my blood.

00:05:16.990 --> 00:05:36.149
Well then, it'd be ashamed to spill it.

00:05:36.149 --> 00:05:38.149
He'll stop you.

00:05:38.149 --> 00:05:39.149
Not under a red sign.

00:05:39.149 --> 00:05:42.430
Look around you.

00:05:42.430 --> 00:07:02.129
Your blur is dead.

00:07:02.129 --> 00:07:05.129
Tess, tune in the TV to Channel Lois is one thing, but

00:07:05.129 --> 00:07:07.129
sinking your brain waves to hers?

00:07:07.129 --> 00:07:08.129
Yes.

00:07:08.129 --> 00:07:11.129
All we're seeing on the screen are jumbled images.

00:07:11.129 --> 00:07:14.129
To get the answers I'm looking for, I need to plug in.

00:07:14.129 --> 00:07:19.600
I didn't build this technology, okay?

00:07:19.600 --> 00:07:22.600
Don't you think we should have someone from SummerHalt here?

00:07:22.600 --> 00:07:25.600
Zad said that his tower is going to change the world.

00:07:25.600 --> 00:07:29.600
Lois' memories to the future should show me how.

00:07:29.600 --> 00:07:32.519
Okay.

00:07:32.519 --> 00:09:08.740
Easy. I was just hoping for some food here, and I'm pretty sure this is a bad dream,

00:09:08.740 --> 00:09:10.740
but right now I could eat about 30 maple donuts.

00:09:10.740 --> 00:09:11.740
You want food?

00:09:11.740 --> 00:09:16.049
and what do you have to trade?

00:09:16.049 --> 00:09:17.049
Take this.

00:09:17.049 --> 00:09:32.389
It's yours if you let her go.

00:09:32.389 --> 00:09:33.389
This will do.

00:09:33.389 --> 00:09:40.659
For now.

00:09:40.659 --> 00:09:43.899
Thank God.

00:09:43.899 --> 00:09:45.899
This dream just got ten times brighter.

00:09:45.899 --> 00:09:46.899
You mean dream.

00:09:46.899 --> 00:09:49.899
Lois, I'm sorry to be the one to tell you this, but you're not dreaming.

00:09:49.899 --> 00:09:56.500
Clark, if this isn't a dream, then it's the worst nightmare I could ever imagine.

00:09:56.500 --> 00:09:59.500
Since when did the Kent Family Farm become a prison?

00:09:59.500 --> 00:10:02.500
And why would you give away the one thing of your dad's that meant so much to you?

00:10:02.500 --> 00:10:08.429
I did it for you.

00:10:08.429 --> 00:10:10.429
Okay, hold on.

00:10:10.429 --> 00:10:13.429
Explain about the wicked witch and the flying freaks.

00:10:13.429 --> 00:10:15.429
Have we been invaded by the Wizard of Oz?

00:10:15.429 --> 00:10:16.429
More like another planet.

00:10:16.429 --> 00:10:18.809
Aliens?

00:10:18.809 --> 00:10:22.409
Clark, before I fought Tess.

00:10:22.409 --> 00:10:23.409
She went on.

00:10:23.409 --> 00:10:27.409
and on about some orb, called it alien technology, said there was life inside of it?

00:10:27.409 --> 00:10:30.409
This invasion, Tess knew about it.

00:10:30.409 --> 00:10:32.409
Tess lived out.

00:10:32.409 --> 00:10:35.409
These aliens have their own leaders, his name Zod.

00:10:35.409 --> 00:10:37.409
I tried to fight it, but...

00:10:37.409 --> 00:10:41.549
I made all the wrong choices.

00:10:41.549 --> 00:10:45.759
A lot of people died.

00:10:45.759 --> 00:10:47.759
Please tell me, Chloe, I wasn't one of them.

00:10:47.759 --> 00:10:51.389
Lois, I don't know.

00:10:51.389 --> 00:10:53.389
After I thought I lost you.

00:10:53.389 --> 00:10:56.389
I went off of my own. I haven't talked to her in months.

00:10:56.389 --> 00:10:58.389
Once?

00:10:58.389 --> 00:10:59.389
Lois, you vanished.

00:10:59.389 --> 00:11:00.389
A year ago.

00:11:00.389 --> 00:11:05.120
No, I was just throwing down with Tess a few hours ago.

00:11:05.120 --> 00:11:10.830
And then I grabbed that gold ring.

00:11:10.830 --> 00:11:13.269
The Legion ring?

00:11:13.269 --> 00:11:16.269
He must have brought you here when you put it on.

00:11:16.269 --> 00:11:18.269
Do you still have it?

00:11:18.269 --> 00:11:19.269
You?

00:11:19.269 --> 00:11:22.740
Then Lazzad would like to see you.

00:11:22.740 --> 00:12:03.909
Where's Lois?

00:12:03.909 --> 00:12:06.909
Last I heard you dropped her at the hospital.

00:12:06.909 --> 00:12:09.909
Someone moved her, and I know that you had Emile look into her records.

00:12:09.909 --> 00:12:11.909
She's my cousin, Clark.

00:12:11.909 --> 00:12:13.909
Chloe, you've been hiding things for me for months.

00:12:13.909 --> 00:12:15.909
Now I think you're hiding Lois.

00:12:15.909 --> 00:12:20.259
Right? Accusation. Wrong girl.

00:12:20.259 --> 00:12:24.259
Clerk, I may not have been sharing my deep, dark secrets with you lately,

00:12:24.259 --> 00:12:29.600
but someone else has been playing hide-and-seek a lot longer than I have.

00:12:29.600 --> 00:12:30.600
Tess.

00:12:30.600 --> 00:12:33.600
Yeah. We can work on your apology later.

00:12:33.600 --> 00:12:38.600
Tess has been keeping more than just an editorial eye on Lois for the past few months.

00:12:38.600 --> 00:12:41.600
Lois can't answer any of her questions. She's in a coma.

00:12:41.600 --> 00:12:44.600
She doesn't have to talk to Tess for her to run tests on her.

00:12:44.600 --> 00:12:47.600
And we both know how obsessed she's been with the fact that Lois vanished for three weeks.

00:12:47.600 --> 00:12:48.600
for three weeks.

00:12:48.600 --> 00:12:53.330
You think this is something to do with her trip to the future?

00:12:53.330 --> 00:12:55.330
I think it's possible.

00:12:55.330 --> 00:12:57.330
Emile gave me the hospital workups on her.

00:12:57.330 --> 00:13:00.330
She suffers from post-traumatic stress disorder.

00:13:00.330 --> 00:13:04.330
Every time she has a memory, her body relives a trauma.

00:13:04.330 --> 00:13:06.330
Her heart can only take so much.

00:13:06.330 --> 00:13:08.330
Chloe, I have to find her.

00:13:08.330 --> 00:13:10.330
Tess is never going to admit that she took Lois.

00:13:10.330 --> 00:13:11.330
Let me try something.

00:13:11.330 --> 00:13:13.330
I have a guy in the inside.

00:13:13.330 --> 00:13:19.179
Okay, ladies, we're a little touch and go here right now,

00:13:19.179 --> 00:13:21.179
but we are stable again.

00:13:21.179 --> 00:13:22.179
And you should have a little bit.

00:13:22.179 --> 00:13:24.179
the front row seat to Lois Manet.

00:13:24.179 --> 00:13:30.549
No, no, no, no, no, no, no, no.

00:13:30.549 --> 00:13:43.720
I guess membership passes, privileges.

00:13:43.720 --> 00:13:45.720
Tried the truffle.

00:13:45.720 --> 00:13:47.720
It's my favorite.

00:13:47.720 --> 00:14:03.879
To think, a few of these could mean the difference

00:14:03.879 --> 00:14:19.549
between life and death for your kind.

00:14:19.549 --> 00:14:21.549
I'm General Zod.

00:14:21.549 --> 00:14:25.549
And all of this is mine to give.

00:14:25.549 --> 00:14:28.549
If you give me the names whoever snuck you into the restricted zone.

00:14:28.549 --> 00:14:32.470
My dad's a general, too.

00:14:32.470 --> 00:14:33.470
Oh.

00:14:33.470 --> 00:14:39.470
And he still couldn't get me to spill how I got an M1 Abrams tank to take me to prom.

00:14:39.470 --> 00:14:42.470
So I'm definitely not telling you anything.

00:14:42.470 --> 00:14:52.700
How many times your resistance fighters break into the zone?

00:14:52.700 --> 00:14:53.700
Never.

00:14:53.700 --> 00:15:14.580
Lois?

00:15:14.580 --> 00:15:22.659
You? You red-head?

00:15:22.659 --> 00:15:25.169
Do you know her?

00:15:25.169 --> 00:15:27.169
She used to work for me.

00:15:27.169 --> 00:15:34.669
But then she disappeared.

00:15:34.669 --> 00:15:36.669
I am this planet's savior.

00:15:36.669 --> 00:15:39.669
I helped General Azad take power to ensure

00:15:39.669 --> 00:15:41.669
this Earth's survival.

00:15:41.669 --> 00:15:43.669
Tess Mercer, the ultimate eco-terrorist.

00:15:43.669 --> 00:15:47.460
And what are you?

00:15:47.460 --> 00:15:49.460
I understand you were seen talking to Clark Ken.

00:15:49.460 --> 00:15:53.460
It was only a matter of time before the resistance got to him.

00:15:53.460 --> 00:15:57.460
The only thing I'm resisting is the urge to kick both your asses.

00:15:57.460 --> 00:16:00.460
And if Clark were here right now, he would back me up.

00:16:00.460 --> 00:16:03.460
The only reason Clark is still alive is because I'd hoped he'd join us

00:16:03.460 --> 00:16:06.460
to bridge the gap between our people.

00:16:06.460 --> 00:16:08.460
Trust me, Zod.

00:16:08.460 --> 00:16:11.460
No one has worked as hard as I have to get clear.

00:16:11.460 --> 00:16:13.460
to see the good that we're doing.

00:16:13.460 --> 00:16:15.460
But I think we've fooled ourselves long enough.

00:16:15.460 --> 00:16:18.809
He won't come around.

00:16:18.809 --> 00:16:24.190
Which is why.

00:16:24.190 --> 00:16:31.960
Neither of you is any good to me alive.

00:16:31.960 --> 00:16:39.570
Double execution will send out a strong message to anyone

00:16:39.570 --> 00:16:41.570
who would dare to find me.

00:16:41.570 --> 00:16:50.669
And take our Lois.

00:16:50.669 --> 00:16:54.669
At least you can enjoy a glorious last meal.

00:16:54.669 --> 00:17:19.720
Today, two lives end.

00:17:19.720 --> 00:17:21.720
But another begins.

00:17:21.720 --> 00:17:46.500
Rice, soldier.

00:17:46.500 --> 00:17:48.500
You betrayed the entire human race for us.

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:50.500
crappy dog tags. Way to go.

00:17:50.500 --> 00:17:56.029
Lois, let her go.

00:17:56.029 --> 00:17:58.029
Take my life, let her live.

00:17:58.029 --> 00:18:05.130
Your bravery is commendable.

00:18:05.130 --> 00:18:08.130
But by defying me, you have forced my hand.

00:18:08.130 --> 00:18:23.180
Join me on this new earth.

00:18:23.180 --> 00:18:27.490
Now I must bury you beneath it.

00:18:27.490 --> 00:19:16.890
Legs. Long time, no sea.

00:19:16.890 --> 00:19:20.890
And am I glad to see you in your band of Mary Men?

00:19:20.890 --> 00:19:22.890
It's not my band.

00:19:22.890 --> 00:19:23.890
What?

00:19:23.890 --> 00:19:24.890
It's hers.

00:19:24.890 --> 00:19:27.650
Chloe.

00:19:27.650 --> 00:19:28.650
I don't think I was ever.

00:19:28.650 --> 00:19:30.150
going to see her again.

00:19:30.150 --> 00:19:31.150
You almost didn't.

00:19:31.150 --> 00:19:34.650
Those crazy space invaders almost killed us.

00:19:34.650 --> 00:19:50.700
I guess we all you guys are lives.

00:19:50.700 --> 00:19:53.700
You always were a good shot.

00:19:53.700 --> 00:19:55.700
I didn't do this to you.

00:19:55.700 --> 00:19:57.700
I didn't.

00:19:57.700 --> 00:19:59.700
No, I did this to myself.

00:19:59.700 --> 00:20:04.700
It was a risk choosing Zad of my own people.

00:20:04.700 --> 00:20:07.700
But someone had to save the Earth.

00:20:07.700 --> 00:20:45.089
I had the shot.

00:20:45.089 --> 00:21:43.059
I had to take him.

00:21:43.059 --> 00:21:44.059
I'm not sure what you saw in there.

00:21:44.059 --> 00:21:46.059
But out here, you were still last.

00:21:46.059 --> 00:21:50.299
So I guess I did okay, right?

00:21:50.299 --> 00:21:53.299
You did your job, Mensa Boy, now finish it.

00:21:53.299 --> 00:21:55.299
I don't want Lewis waking up with the memories that I just saw.

00:21:55.299 --> 00:21:56.299
That would be too dangerous.

00:21:56.299 --> 00:21:58.299
Use the device to wipe them out.

00:21:58.299 --> 00:22:01.299
Tess, if I make a mistake, she could come out of this catatonic.

00:22:01.299 --> 00:22:18.980
Don't argue with me, Stuart.

00:22:18.980 --> 00:22:21.980
No. Okay, I won't do it.

00:22:21.980 --> 00:22:22.980
I won't.

00:22:22.980 --> 00:22:23.980
Excuse me?

00:22:23.980 --> 00:22:25.980
I'm gonna pull her out, Tess.

00:22:25.980 --> 00:22:29.980
I'm sorry, but we are literally messing with someone's mind here.

00:22:29.980 --> 00:22:35.390
I'm sorry too.

00:22:35.390 --> 00:22:46.000
Clark.

00:22:46.000 --> 00:22:48.000
Stewart went rogue.

00:22:48.000 --> 00:22:50.000
He took her. I had to stop him.

00:22:50.000 --> 00:22:51.000
You do to her.

00:22:51.000 --> 00:23:08.150
We may have won the battle, but Zod will come back harder now.

00:23:08.150 --> 00:23:10.150
It's time we take a stand.

00:23:10.150 --> 00:23:13.150
Lois vanished a year ago after she put on the Legion ring.

00:23:13.150 --> 00:23:15.150
You time traveled here?

00:23:15.150 --> 00:23:19.150
I'm pretty sure I didn't walk a whole year into the future, not in these heels.

00:23:19.150 --> 00:23:21.150
The thing is, I lost the ring.

00:23:21.150 --> 00:23:23.150
That one named Wunder Zod took it.

00:23:23.150 --> 00:23:25.150
We need to get the ring back.

00:23:25.150 --> 00:23:26.150
Then Lois can return to the past.

00:23:26.150 --> 00:23:27.150
Then Lois can return to the past.

00:23:27.150 --> 00:23:29.150
and prevent Zod's tower from being built in the first place.

00:23:29.150 --> 00:23:32.150
That's not a bad plan, Clark, but why should I trust you now?

00:23:32.150 --> 00:23:34.150
You already left us once to fight on your own.

00:23:34.150 --> 00:23:39.069
You abandon us, big guy, plain and simple.

00:23:39.069 --> 00:23:41.069
I thought I could stop Zod myself.

00:23:41.069 --> 00:23:43.069
I tried to take him on as my enemy, and I was wrong.

00:23:43.069 --> 00:23:45.069
But I'm here now.

00:23:45.069 --> 00:23:49.069
Okay, then look, why Clark decided to take on our enemy ETs,

00:23:49.069 --> 00:23:51.069
by himself is beyond me.

00:23:51.069 --> 00:23:54.069
And maybe you think he abandoned the cause or something.

00:23:54.069 --> 00:23:56.069
But come on, aren't we all in this together?

00:23:56.069 --> 00:23:59.069
You guys shut down that tower and bring back the yellow sun?

00:23:59.069 --> 00:24:01.069
You know I'm your best chance of getting back that ring.

00:24:01.069 --> 00:24:03.930
Maybe.

00:24:03.930 --> 00:24:05.930
I still don't trust you.

00:24:05.930 --> 00:24:10.519
I guess that's a start.

00:24:10.519 --> 00:24:12.519
So about the tower?

00:24:12.519 --> 00:24:14.519
The towers are the key to the Kandorian's power.

00:24:14.519 --> 00:24:16.519
They collect all the sun's radiation, turn it red,

00:24:16.519 --> 00:24:18.519
and then beam it back up to the Luther Corp.

00:24:18.519 --> 00:24:19.519
Satellites.

00:24:19.519 --> 00:24:22.519
Those satellites take the radiation, they beam it back down to Earth.

00:24:22.519 --> 00:24:25.519
Even those alien SOBs, all their superhuman strength.

00:24:25.519 --> 00:24:28.519
Now we take the tower down, shut them down.

00:24:28.519 --> 00:24:30.519
Guys, I've seen Zod's troops.

00:24:30.519 --> 00:24:32.519
We are seriously outnumbered. We'd never reach it.

00:24:32.519 --> 00:24:33.519
We don't have you.

00:24:33.519 --> 00:24:34.519
to.

00:24:34.519 --> 00:24:37.519
We have a secret weapon, watchtower.

00:24:37.519 --> 00:24:40.519
